  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/callichthyidae/corydoras_geoffroy.htm",
      "html": "<p>Corydoras geoffroy La Cépède, 1803. Family: Callichthyidae. Size: male 6.5 cm, female 7.0 cm. Temperature: 23–26°C. pH: 6.0–7.2.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/callichthyidae/corydoras_geoffroy.htm",
      "html": "<p>South America: coastal rivers of Suriname and French Guiana. Type locality: Suriname, district Brokopondo, Suriname River system, Marchall Creek, east of the road Paranam-Afobaka, 1.5 km north of Marchall village.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/corydoras-geoffroy-4/",
      "html": "<p>Corydoras geoffroy comes from the Guyana countries Suriname and French Guyana, from where there are no ornamental fish exports. The species, described as early as 1803, could therefore only be made available to the hobby by adventurous traveling aquarists. Since 2018, Corydoras specialists have been successfully engaged in breeding these unusual animals.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/callichthyidae/corydoras_geoffroy.htm",
      "html": "<p>As this is one of the longer snouted species it will be well suited to most community tanks. A well planted tank with a soft substrate such as sand so they can bury their snouts while searching out food. The males can be somewhat aggressive to each other so would need a large tank and hiding places to dilute this trait.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/callichthyidae/corydoras_geoffroy.htm",
      "html": "<p>A good quality flake food and tablet food for adults with sporadic feedings of frozen or live food will keep your Corydoras in good health.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/callichthyidae/corydoras_geoffroy.htm",
      "html": "<p>This is the type species of the Corydoras genus. This species also has a third rictal barbel, also found in C. amapaensis, C. septentrionalis and C. simulatus. Lineage: placed in Lineage 1; following the latest update (Dias et al 2024) it has retained the genus name Corydoras. Etymology: the specific name geoffroy honours colleague Étienne Geoffroy Saint-Hilaire (1772–1844), French naturalist. IUCN Red List: classified as Least Concern (LC) (IUCN 2023); there are no known threats to the species as a whole.</p>"
    }
  ],
